  "name": "24 HR URINARY METANEPHRINES",
  "code": "1155",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><strong>Comment</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Metanephrine and normetanephrine are collectively called as metanephrines which are urinary metabolic products from catecholamines catabolism pathway</li>\n<li>Elevated levels of metanephrines are associated with catecholamine secreting tumors of chromaffin cells like<br>pheochromocytomas, paragangliomas and neuroblastomas.</li>\n<li>Clinical diagnosis should not be made on the findings of a single test result, but should integrate both clinical and&nbsp;laboratory data.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Kindly note</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Caffeine intake before or during collection process can lead to fluctuation in the levels</li>\n<li>False positive results can occur from stress and drugs like amphetamines, appetite suppressants, bromocriptine,&nbsp;caffeine, dexamethasone, diuretics, methyldopa, nasal drops, propafenone, tri cyclic antidepressants, buspirone etc.</li>\n<li>Monoamine Oxidase Inhibitor drug needs to be stopped 1 week priorto collection</li>\n</ul>",
